WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- At this point in the show,

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.640
I always love to share something

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.960
that I'm lovin' on social media.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.160
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.745
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:07.967
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.967 --> 00:00:10.470
So if you have a dog or have ever had one,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.600
you know that you're
constantly trying to teach them

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.560
and train them

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.140
but you may not actually know
how much dogs can teach us.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.380
So a New Jersey veterinarian
says that she learned a lot

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.300
from pups as she was battling cancer.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.490
And now she's written a
self-help book about it

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.800
and it's called "Sit, Stay, Heal."

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.940
Great title.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.320
We have her on the line right now.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.736
Let's say hello to Dr. Renee,
watching on NBC4 New York.

00:00:31.736 --> 00:00:33.660
(audience applauds)

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.710
- Hi, Dr. Renee.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.350
So first of all, tell
us about your diagnosis

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.760
and how you're feeling today.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.593
- Okay.

00:00:39.593 --> 00:00:42.120
Thank you, Kelly, for having me on.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.960
I was diagnosed with cancer in 2018,

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.690
and in fact, I am the poster child

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.840
for why we all need to go
get checked every single year

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.060
because I had no clinical signs.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.170
Unfortunately, at my
gynecology yearly appointment,

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.290
my doctor noticed a
small mass in my uterus

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.110
which was uterine cancer.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.840
Since that time, I've had surgery,

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.650
numerous months of chemotherapy
and radiation therapy.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.320
But thankfully, right
now my doctors are using

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.750
the good C word or "cure."

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:20.130
I don't wanna jinx myself or
the universe but I'm doing well

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.680
and they don't need to see
me back for a whole year.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.390
- That's incredible.
(audience applauds)

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.030
Congratulations on that.

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:29.400
And you say that your dog
and the dogs that you treat

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.540
helped you get through this.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.440
How so?

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.440
- So I have been a
veterinarian for 30 years

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.660
and I've always learned from my patients

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.540
but especially when I had cancer.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.090
For me, my treatment was hard,

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.210
but my dog looked at me with such love,

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.890
which gave me strength.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.200
He didn't judge me.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.400
I also knew-

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.110
During my treatment, I would worry

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:55.440
that perhaps the chemotherapy
nurse couldn't hit my vein.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.910
But dogs don't do that.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:00.570
They don't use their
energy to fret or to worry.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.240
They only use it for positive things.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.820
So I put all of that in my book,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.730
truly life lessons from dogs,

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.786
helping us to all hopefully live happier.

00:02:11.786 --> 00:02:13.200
- It's so important.
(audience applauds)

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.090
Yeah, you go through something
and share it with the world

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.160
and connect with other people
that might need that message.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.290
So thank you so much Dr. Renee.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.195
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:02:21.195 --> 00:02:22.080
(audience applauds)

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.183
- Thank you.

00:02:23.183 --> 00:02:24.387
(heart emoji pings)

00:02:24.387 --> 00:02:25.500
- All right, everybody.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.930
So we've reached the end of the show

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.570
and we have something special
for someone in the audience

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.040
courtesy of our season-long partner

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.900
Pilot pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.700
the go-to erasable pin of
the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.450
So there's a check for $1,000

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.070
under one of your chairs, taped.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.005
So look.

00:02:42.005 --> 00:02:45.401
(drumroll music)

00:02:45.401 --> 00:02:47.880
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:48.713
Who's got it?

00:02:48.713 --> 00:02:49.546
Who's going shopping?

00:02:49.546 --> 00:02:50.379
Yay!

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:53.454
(audience applauds)

00:02:54.308 --> 00:02:55.406
- Hey.
- Hello.

00:02:55.406 --> 00:02:57.074
- What in the world?

00:02:57.074 --> 00:02:57.907
- What's your-

00:02:57.907 --> 00:02:58.992
What's your name?

00:02:58.992 --> 00:03:01.110
- I'm Lily and I'm the
biggest fan of you, Kelly.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:01.943
What the heck?

00:03:01.943 --> 00:03:05.070
Oh my God, this is crazy.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:05.903
- I love it.

00:03:05.903 --> 00:03:07.260
How do you think you're
gonna spend that money?

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.334
- Concert tickets.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:09.167
- Yeah.
(Lily laughs)

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.282
(audience applauds)

00:03:10.282 --> 00:03:11.880
What a great answer.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.500
- And I've never seen you in concert

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.900
so maybe if there's a show
sometime down the road.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.788
- I don't know, maybe there
might be one coming on.

00:03:17.788 --> 00:03:18.900
I dunno.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.547
I can't say it so...

00:03:20.547 --> 00:03:21.380
But you might be able to use it.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.160
I'm gonna plan for that.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.743
So anyway, can't let
the cat outta the bag.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.270
Thank you so much and I
hope you enjoy the money.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.690
(audience applauds)
- Thank you!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.476
- Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:32.476 --> 00:03:35.370
Ike Barinholtz, Sarah
Ferguson, the Duchess of York,

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.570
and all members of Twice.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:40.930
Y'all have a great day.
(audience applauds)

